Input: novatek-nvt-ts: initialise when the panel is prepared (drm_panel_follower) instead of polling for 30 s

The NT36672A controller is powered from the panel bias rail and only answers once the panel is up. The local patch worked around that with a delayed work that polled the I2C bus every 200 ms for up to 30 s. Use the standard DRM panel-follower mechanism (as i2c-hid and goodix do): with a "panel" phandle in the touchscreen node the init runs from panel_prepared(); without one it initialises immediately. DT: touchscreen@1 gets panel = <&panel0>. #187: "Detected 1080x2340 touchscreen" at 5.96 s, immediately after the panel.

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/novatek-nvt-ts.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/novatek-nvt-ts.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <drm/drm_panel.h>
 #include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/i2c.h>
